=== ISSUE ===
Title: npm hygiene: audit findings, version in three places, full build on every install

- `npm audit` reports 9 vulnerabilities (1 critical, 4 high), including the MCP SDK and its HTTP stack.
- The version 0.2.0 is written in package.json, src/server.ts and src/ui/shared/app-bootstrap.ts, so a bump can miss one.
- `prepare` runs the full build (typecheck, three Vite builds, tsc) on every `npm install`/`npm ci`. CI and the Dockerfile already pass --ignore-scripts to dodge it.

=== PR ===
Title: chore: npm audit fixes, a single source for the version, no build on install
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- `npm audit fix`, plus vite 8.3 and vitest 5. Runtime dependencies: 0 vulnerabilities. One dev-only finding is left: braces (via vite-plugin-singlefile's micromatch) has no patched release; it runs at build time on our own files.
- The server reads its version from package.json via createRequire; the UI imports it, and Vite inlines only the string.
- `prepare` is removed. The README's manual install already has an explicit build step. Installing straight from git now needs `npm run build`.
- vite.config.ts uses import.meta.dirname (Vite 8.3 warns about __dirname).
- Coverage under vitest 5 reads 60% overall vs 79% under vitest 3, with no test removed: the v8 coverage remapping changed. Mention this so it isn't read as a regression.

Commits: test first (fails on main: version hard-coded), then the fix, then the dependency and prepare chores.
Verification: 397/397 tests pass, build clean. Docker smoke test: runs in CI.

